# Fixes the `playwright run-server` process leaking past pest's own exit
# (tracked separately by tools/pest-cleanup.sh, which force-kills whatever
# leaked -- this patch fixes the actual cause instead of only cleaning up
# after it).
#
# PlaywrightNpmServer::start() launches the server via
# SystemProcess::fromShellCommandline(), which hands proc_open() a plain
# command *string*. Symfony's Process only prefixes such a string with
# `exec` (replacing the shell instead of forking under it) when
# Process::isSigchildEnabled() is true -- a check for PHP's old
# `--enable-sigchild` build flag. Confirmed live in this project's PHP
# build that flag is NOT set, so that branch never runs, and proc_open()
# falls through to its plain string-command path, which always invokes
# `/bin/sh -c "<command>"`. On this system /bin/sh forks rather than
# exec'ing a single simple command, so Symfony ends up tracking the PID
# of the *shell*, not `playwright run-server` itself -- confirmed by
# directly reproducing Symfony's exact proc_open() call and inspecting
# /proc: the tracked PID's own cmdline is `sh -c ./node_modules/.bin/
# playwright run-server ...`, with the real `node ... run-server` process
# as its untracked child.
#
# PlaywrightNpmServer::stop() then calls Symfony Process::stop(), which
# SIGTERMs the tracked PID (the shell) and gets back a clean exit code --
# but SIGTERM sent to a specific PID never cascades to that PID's own
# children, so the real server process is simply orphaned, reparented to
# the nearest subreaper (systemd --user in this environment), and keeps
# running/listening indefinitely.
#
# The fix: construct SystemProcess from an argv *array* instead of a
# shell string. For an array command, proc_open() execve()s the binary
# directly with no shell involved at all, so the PID Symfony tracks IS
# the real `playwright run-server` process, and stop()'s SIGTERM reaches
# it directly. explode(' ', ...) is safe here specifically because every
# argument in this one hardcoded command template (host/port/mode) is a
# plain unquoted token with no embedded spaces -- this is not a
# general-purpose shell-argument parser.
#
# Matches the (still open, unmerged as of this patch) upstream fix in
# https://github.com/pestphp/pest-plugin-browser/pull/169, though that
# PR's own stated diagnosis ("the shell... does not forward [the signal]
# to playwright") turned out to be imprecise for this exact mechanism --
# real-world confirmation here required directly inspecting /proc, not
# just re-reading the PR's own reasoning. Deliberately does not port that
# PR's second, unrelated "avoid persisting a new port if playwright is
# already set" change to ServerManager.php -- our installed 4.3.1 already
# has a materially different playwright() method (a Playwright::host()
# lookup the PR's base version didn't have), and that second change isn't
# needed for this fix.
--- a/src/Playwright/Servers/PlaywrightNpmServer.php	2026-07-27 20:06:38.609019600 -0300
+++ b/src/Playwright/Servers/PlaywrightNpmServer.php	2026-07-27 20:06:48.627453065 -0300
@@ -60,11 +60,11 @@
             return;
         }
 
-        $this->systemProcess = SystemProcess::fromShellCommandline(sprintf(
+        $this->systemProcess = new SystemProcess(explode(' ', sprintf(
             $this->command,
             $this->host,
             $this->port,
-        ), $this->baseDirectory, [
+        )), $this->baseDirectory, [
             'APP_URL' => sprintf('http://%s:%d', $this->host, $this->port),
         ]);
 
